nabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a deterministic post-repair integrity check (e.g. server `git fsck --full` returns clean and the tree resolves) as the proving evidence for the restoration criterion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The criterion asserts restoration but no post-repair verification check is described in the Investigation plan beyond 'verify ordinary review upload and receive-pack health'.","No concrete integrity command (git fsck exit 0 / object-count) is stated."],"finding":"The criterion 'Repository integrity is restored through a backed-up, supported recovery procedure' has no verification command (e.g. server-side fsck clean, successful reachability walk) proving integrity was actually restored.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5a0e3459ab902fdb","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'Repository integrity is restored through a backed-up, supported recovery procedure'","norm_id":"nced6f000d5bd4a13","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Repair appears to succeed but latent object-store corruption remains undetected."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Record post-repair `git fsck --full` clean output and `git cat-file -t <tree>` on the server as proving evidence.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Document the explicit back-out step (snapshot the repo before any write, and the exact restore command to revert if repair corrupts refs/changes or main).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4","T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.701,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan references a backup ('backed-up, supported recovery path') but states no rollback/restore-from-snapshot procedure if the repair worsens the object store.","'no review data is lost' is a required end-state with no described mechanism to revert a failed repair."],"finding":"Server repository repair is a destructive/irreversible operation, and while a backup is mentioned, there is no explicit back-out plan for the case where the recovery itself further corrupts refs/changes or main.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc60df54ffc82ba78","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Investigation plan / Acceptance Criteria — 'through a backed-up, supported recovery path'; 'Existing refs/changes and main remain valid and no review data is lost'","norm_id":"n33f9ad87ccbe22da","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A repack/gc during repair prunes a still-referenced object; refs/changes become unreachable and must be restored."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add: take a full filesystem/repo snapshot before any repair write; if post-repair fsck fails or refs are lost, restore from that snapshot and abort.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concurrency/ownership controls for the repair window (quiesce the Gerrit repo / pause replication / block writes) so no concurrent push or replication can be lost or re-corrupt the object store during recovery.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan states 'Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path, then verify ordinary review upload and receive-pack health.'","AC: 'Existing refs/changes and main remain valid and no review data is lost' — asserts the outcome but the plan does not specify the concurrency/ownership controls that guarantee it during the repair window.","ABSENCE: no mention of quiescing the repo, pausing replication, or serializing writes while the recovery runs."],"finding":"The plan mutates shared server state (the Gerrit repository object store and refs) via 'repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path' but does not state how concurrent access is handled during the repair — whether the repository is quiesced/taken offline, replication paused, or in-flight pushes blocked. A repair applied while pushes or replication run concurrently can corrupt the object graph or lose the very refs the plan promises to preserve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5db0c0e7e91f9468","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Investigation plan: 'Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path'","norm_id":"ndbe480a791284d4f","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A push or replication event lands on the Gerrit repo mid-repair, so a newly created ref/change written after the backup snapshot is silently dropped by the restore — violating 'no review data is lost'."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a step that takes the repository read-only or offline (and pauses replication) for the recovery window, and reconciles any refs written after the backup snapshot before re-enabling writes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a positive rationale for the chosen repair path and confirm it against lower-blast-radius alternatives (re-replicate from a healthy replica/mirror, or fsck-guided targeted object recovery), choosing the option that repairs the named tree without reverting post-backup refs/changes.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path, then verify ordinary review upload and receive-pack health.'","Plan quote (inspection step): 'Verify Gerrit's main ref, reachable object graph, alternates/promisor configuration, recent replication, and repository consistency' — names replication, implying a peer that could serve as a lower-blast-radius repair source.","ABSENCE: no sentence in the plan states why backup/recovery was chosen over re-replication or targeted object recovery."],"finding":"The plan commits to repairing via 'the supported backup/recovery path' but states no positive rationale for choosing it over other supported repairs (re-replicating the repository from a healthy replica/mirror, or an fsck-guided targeted object recovery). Since the plan itself lists 'recent replication' as an inspection target — implying a healthier peer may exist — a full backup-restore is not obviously the best-fit or lowest-blast-radius repair, and its rationale is unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90c3e591e95372a3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Investigation plan — 'Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path'","norm_id":"n28c86301c5b6268a","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A healthy Gerrit replica/mirror holds the missing tree, so re-replicating the affected repo would restore integrity without a full restore.","fsck identifies a bounded set of missing/corrupt objects that could be re-imported directly, avoiding a whole-repo rollback."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the repair step, add why the chosen path fits (e.g. 'no healthy replica retains the missing objects, so restore-then-replay is the only supported recovery') and, if a replica/mirror does hold the tree, prefer re-replication or targeted object recovery over a full backup-restore to satisfy the no-data-loss acceptance criterion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name and verify the concrete server-side commands/procedure for log inspection and object-store repair (e.g., git fsck/repack/gc, JGit consistency check, Gerrit `gerrit gc`, and the specific backup/restore mechanism) against Gerrit/git docs, classifying each as MATCH/UNVERIFIED.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path, then verify ordinary review upload and receive-pack health.'","Plan quote: 'inspect the receive-pack/JGit